index c51e0950cd2..9c67ed8be3d 100644
--- a/apps/desktop/DESIGN.md
+++ b/apps/desktop/DESIGN.md
@@ -1,5 +1,39 @@
 # Desktop Design System
 
+## Jarvis voice controls
+
+Keep voice activation, listen-only mode and capture pause in one compact toolbar.
+Secondary tools live in the Ferramentas popover; check-in notices remain indicated
+on its trigger. Music playback lives outside that popover so closing it never
+stops playback. In face mode, the toolbar and message form occupy separate rows
+inside one 16px console. Tool forms must never nest inside the message form.
+In chat, use a small portrait beside the toolbar and a subdued galaxy backdrop
+(18% opacity), keeping the transcript and composer primary. Preserve the full
+galaxy and supplied portrait in face mode. Use the existing UI color tokens.
+
+## Jarvis face reference
+
+The full-screen face follows __JARVIS_USER__'s supplied galaxy portrait: midnight blue,
+violet and muted orange-to-rose nebulae, cyan memory hubs, warm stars and a friendly cyan-blue holographic
+head. Preserve the supplied blue portrait colors independently of the galaxy palette.
+Keep the head centred below the memory cloud, with the dock at the bottom.
+The supplied illustration defines the character's geometry, palette and mood.
+Use the exact transparent `fixed-portrait.png` supplied by __JARVIS_USER__ as a fixed
+frontal 2D illustration. Preserve its aspect ratio, ears, neck, circuits and colors.
+The portrait never turns or responds to pointer movement. Keep it translucent,
+small (up to 280px tall) and close to the chat, as in the supplied layout screenshot.
+Animate the original eyelid and lip pixels locally. Upper and lower lips move
+independently around the original recessed seam, with fixed mouth corners and
+restrained movement of the lower face. Drive articulation from playback amplitude;
+silence closes the mouth. Blink at irregular intervals. Do not add an oval mouth.
+Preserve the entire galaxy renderer and appearance; only its initial camera
+distance changes to 0.9 to match the supplied zoomed-in screenshot.
+Anchor the portrait just above the chat and its replies without a fixed upward jump.
+The face animates the mouth only during voice playback. Approaching memories shrinks the
+portrait smoothly; returning restores its original size. Apply zoom directly
+to the portrait element without rendering the React tree on every frame.
+
+
 Conventions for the Electron desktop app (`apps/desktop`). Read this before
 adding a component, overlay, or style. The rule of thumb: **one source per
 concern, tokens over literals, flat over boxed.** If you reach for a raw color,
@@ -574,3 +608,25 @@ The detailed state contract lives in the scoped
 - [ ] `cursor-pointer`, focus ring, and `Esc`-to-close behave?
 - [ ] Touched a primitive, token, or variant? Its named-contract entry in this
       file is updated in the same change.
+
+## Jarvis normal workspace
+
+Reuse the fixed frontal portrait and galaxy from face mode. The normal chat
+keeps its transcript, composer and pane navigation. Use one small portrait
+in the voice dock and a larger portrait for the empty conversation. No hardware,
+version, weather or idle online badges. Only real activity and voice errors
+appear in the quiet header. Opening face mode preserves the normal composer.
+
+Workspace tokens: `--jarvis-workspace-night` (#080b1b),
+`--jarvis-workspace-text` (#eef0fa), `--jarvis-workspace-muted` (#aeb5cd),
+`--jarvis-workspace-stroke` (#ffffff14). Nebula accents reuse face ember and violet.
+Use the dark wash for text contrast. Decorative canvases never capture input.
+Suspend the workspace galaxy when hidden, inactive, or covered by face mode.
+Reduced motion uses the static nebula fallback. Keep the native HUD transparent.
+Normal-window chrome, sidebars, menus and the composer use the workspace dark
+palette even when a previous installation saved a light theme. This is a scoped
+visual contract, not a write to the user's persisted appearance preferences.
+In existing conversations, place the portrait above the voice toolbar on the
+transparent galaxy, at 160px high (120px for windows up to 900px wide or 700px
+high). Keep it in the measured composer dock so the transcript reserves its
+space and the voice toolbar retains its own compact height.
