+++ b/apps/desktop/src/lib/jarvis-face/assets/SCULPT.md
@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@
+# Reference head
+
+The source `reference-head.glb` was reconstructed from the user-approved `reference-face.png` by the official Microsoft TRELLIS.2 service on 2026-10-07. It is actual volumetric geometry, including ears, nose, cheeks, lips and the rear of the skull. No front-facing photo is rendered over another head.
+
+`humanoid-rig.bin` is generated by `scripts/rig-reconstructed.py` (Python, numpy and trimesh, development tooling only). It removes detached reconstruction artifacts, smooths coincident UV seams, splits the existing lip seam and builds recessed mouth geometry plus jaw/lid deformation targets. JRI2 uses 24 float32 values per vertex and uint32 triangle indices. The renderer adds a translucent warm holographic surface and a fading crown.
+
+To regenerate, use the isolated modeling Python environment under Hermes tools. No external service is contacted by the running application.
